// numbered cases with several paragraphs each, closed by "in either case"
let p be a prime. wts p = 2 or p is odd
case 1 p = 2.
then the claim holds trivially.

there is nothing more to show here.
case 2 p != 2.
suppose p is even. then 2 | p, and since p is prime, p = 2, a contradiction.

hence p is odd.
in either case, p = 2 or p is odd.
qed
